    "evidence_text": " It appears on the 1965 Andy Williams album, \"Andy Williams' Dear Heart\".\n\n It was recorded and released that year by pop singer Andy Williams for his first Christmas album, \"The Andy Williams Christmas Album\".\n\nAndy Williams' Greatest Hits\n\nAndy Williams' Greatest Hits is a compilation album by American pop singer Andy Williams that was released in early 1970 by Columbia Records.\n\nAndy Williams Sings Steve Allen\n\nHark! The Herald Angels Sing\n\n\"Hark!\n\n The Herald Angels Sing\" is a Christmas carol that first appeared in 1739 in the collection \"Hymns and Sacred Poems\", having been written by Charles Wesley.\n\n Wesley had requested and received slow and solemn music for his lyrics, not the joyful tune expected today.\n\n Moreover, Wesley's original opening couplet is \"Hark!\n\n how all the welkin rings / Glory to the King of Kings\".\n\nGet Together with Andy Williams\n\nGet Together with Andy Williams is an album by American pop singer Andy Williams that was released on October 6, 1969, by Columbia Records and contained covers of recent hits.\n\n\"Hawaiian Wedding Song\" is a traditional pop music song recorded by singer Andy Williams in 1959.",
